          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "a painted or stained cloth: a decorative hanging for a room, painted or worked with figures, mottoes or texts (OED s.v. painted 5; cloth, painted); also an awning (pentice / penthouse cloth; Carlin 246). Attested as Latin pannus depictus (panno depicto, pannis depictis, pannorum depictorum, etc.), French drapz depictus, and English paynted/payntid cloth(es) and cloth(es) pictorum (painters' cloth)."
    }
  ],
